A root-relative feed key is a logical membership locator. It need not name a physical projection file under the owner. In particular, ordinary retained batches and unique-slot sources can establish feeds without creating dated or standalone projection files. Facade feed handles remain address values and cannot grant host-root selection or read/write authority. Superseded data/logs resolution still refuses outside the explicit offline migration path.

The `date` selection is one exact date partition, not a timestamp cutoff. Its date is the existing four-digit-year, two-digit-month, two-digit-day address string (`YYYY-MM-DD`, exactly ten ASCII characters). Select memberships whose first three POSIX path components are exactly the corresponding year/month/day and which have a remaining filename component. Do not derive this membership date from each observation's time: a continuing encounter can remain in its original append partition. Preserve the existing address law's unclassified `0000-00-00` partition when it is present; do not silently erase such custody or invent a real calendar date for it. No new timezone/calendar validator is introduced by this storage selection. Undated standalone/custom feeds remain discoverable in territory selections and through their exact feed key; their observation timestamp does not fabricate a dated membership. Unique virtual feeds use the existing address constructor and their specified original observation values.

The facade's through-date and subject-through-date folds retain their separate inclusive lexical partition cutoff and existing subject address law. They select the entire relevant feed union under one owner scope, establish completeness for that union before the first callback, then traverse it once in causal order. Do not perform independently protected per-feed reads and combine them into an apparently consistent territory observation. An unrelated pending feed excluded by that selection does not prevent the selected complete fold. Every retained feed remains in territory membership even if no dated projection exists.

As-of frontier is a dense ordinary array of valid witness references in strict ordinal increasing order. It is neither a string/other iterable nor a derived-frontier manifest object. Refuse malformed values rather than guessing tips, coercing iterables or silently dropping duplicates. Verify the full required causal closure of every supplied reference against the same protected root view, including causes belonging to other feeds; then intersect verified envelopes with the requested feed and apply the causal order law. Missing, blocked or pending required evidence refuses. Multiple tips may share causes, which appear once. An empty frontier denotes the explicit empty section for this ordinary read API. A domain requiring a nonempty frontier must enforce that stronger requirement at its own boundary. Existing deriveFrontier/closure artifacts are separate pure APIs and do not implicitly change this argument shape.

Receiving must compare settled and standalone address resolution, distinct standalone names and owners, stale-path refusal, cross-feed causes, a missing requested tip, duplicate/string/manifest misuse, exact empty frontier, date-anchor continuity, undated territory visibility and inclusive through-date selection. These contracts refine the generator input; no runtime acceptance follows until the facade, migration and owner implement the same mapping.

## L-O25 — Source-derived reuse without a second causal evaluator

L-S05 requires warm ordinary admission not to reverify the entire unrelated history. L-O22 requires every refreshed logical view to include all current historical decisions before readiness is judged. Satisfy both with a disposable derived view in the owner. Complete bounded discovery still occurs under every protected operation. Read and hash recognized bounded source bytes and compare their exact identities/digests before using cached parsed records. A warm cache never suppresses new, missing, changed or malformed source evidence and never enlarges the configured source/scan budgets.

If the complete verified source and decision sets are unchanged, reuse the immutable parsed records and existing causal substrate. For monotone additions with an unchanged historical-decision set, verify newly discovered source records, retain all feed memberships, and deliver only previously unseen verified artifact source pairs through the existing substrate's receiveSourceSet. Preserve new pending bodies so a later missing dependency triggers the existing fixed point. The substrate alone computes causal state; Systems must not mutate its internal admitted/blocked maps or copy those maps into a new object as an alternative evaluator. Adding a feed membership for an existing witness is a membership change even when no new semantic source is delivered.

On source withdrawal, replacement of an admitted physical binding, changed historical decisions, or an invalidated derived view, discard the affected cached judgment and rebuild from the complete current verified source/decision inputs through rebuildCausalSubstrate. A malformed or identity-conflicting current source refuses rather than becoming an implicit removal. Install all current retained blocking decisions before the reconstruction's first promotion pass. Required acknowledged closure bytes are reread and synchronized under L-O04 even on cache hits. A changed host/root binding still ends the owner lifetime under L-H02; a source refresh cannot follow it into another store.

Thus 'reconstruct from current sources' is a provenance requirement, not an instruction to replay unrelated verification on every ordinary append. Reuse is allowed only when it is equivalent to cold reconstruction of the exact current sources and retained decisions. No persistent index, hidden recovery flag or writable cache file is introduced. Receiving must observe cold/warm equivalence, unchanged-history verification reuse, late dependency recovery, membership-only additions, newly discovered blocks and source withdrawal/alteration; private instrumentation may establish avoided verification without adding production counters or telemetry APIs.
